 but I think  many people looked up today live in the  last hour Brett saw a president of first  lady  truly moved by what they see in the loss  of the senseless loss and the act of  evil there this president has shown up  in Las Vegas and parkland Florida  he's been there for natural disasters  that have struck different states and  territories and and so for him this is  this is more of a natural place for him  to be than people give him credit for by  the other issue today is that he told  Axios that he wants to possibly sign an  executive order to change birthright  citizenship here is how Speaker Paul  Ryan on this issue obviously cannot do  that you cannot end birthright  citizenship with an executive order we  didn't like it when Obama try changing  immigration laws the executive action  and obviously as conservatives you know  we believe in the Constitution as  conservatives we believe in the  Constitution so how do you respond well  as do me well we didn't like it when the  Congress failed to act on immigration  for Oh many years now including this  last year you know it's been over a year  Brett since the president presented his  70 point immigration plan to the United  States Congress they never acted on it  then he boiled it down to four points  take care of the dreamers daca build the  wall and the Visa Lottery and then end  the chain migration four very simple  concepts all of which poll very well by  the way with with large swaths of  Americans not just the base and yet  Congress never acted now on the matter  of birth right citizenship 30 countries  do have it but only two in the quote  developed world as the IMF defines that  Canada in the u.s. Europe doesn't have  that France and there's in 1993  and most parts of Asia many parts of  Asia don't have it so many other  constitutional scholars have said that  the 14th amendment has been  misinterpreted or misused in this way  there's no question that there have been  news reports about for some birth 